<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕtōpĭon</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-um</span></b> , ii, n.
		(also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕ-tops</span></b> ,
			ōpis, <i><span class="en">Sol.
		40</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετώπιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The gum of an African tree, also called</i>
			ammoniacum, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 23, 49, § 107</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 27, 47</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Oil of bitter almonds, almond-oil</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 7,
				7, § 26</span></i> (Jahn, neopum).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An ointment made with galbanum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 1,
				2, § 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
